<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.1;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);1591</NoWarn>

    <Title>Artisan.ORM</Title>
    <Version>4.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Vadim Loboda</Authors>
    <Description>
    ADO.NET Micro-ORM to SQL Server. Multi-targets .NET Standard 2.1, .NET 8 and .NET 10.
    Use version 2.x.x, which was built with .NET Standard 2.0, if you need to use this library with the .NET Framework.

    This library is designed to use stored procedures, table-valued parameters and structured static mappers, with the goal of reading and saving complex object graphs at once in a fast, convenient and efficient way.

    Read more: https://github.com/lobodava/artisan-orm/wiki
    </Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright 2016-2026</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/lobodava/artisan-orm</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageIcon>Logo.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/lobodava/artisan-orm</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>Git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>ado.net orm micro-orm sql server mssql bulkcopy iasyncenumerable</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Artisan.ORM 4.1.0

- Bundled Roslyn mapper diagnostics ART001-ART007, including complete RequiredMethod.AllMain checks.
- Fixed first-row reads, explicit projections, async cancellation, transaction ownership and cleanup.
- Isolated mapper and procedure-parameter caches; preserved complete parameter metadata.
- Corrected string and decimal normalization, dictionary parameter names, and enum auto-mapping.
- Enforced finite negative-ID ranges and disposed MergeJoin enumerators.
- Hardened optional DataReply status validation and exception messages.
- Updated SqlClient and patched vulnerable transitive dependencies.
- Updated sample SQL, articles, wiki, and the Claude Code skill. SQL changes require separate deployment.

Targets: netstandard2.1, net8.0, net10.0. Includes XML documentation, SourceLink, and symbols.
ReadToLists supports two, three, or four result sets.

Compatibility: excess decimal scale is rejected unless truncateFraction is true (truncation toward zero).
Exhausted negative-ID generators throw instead of wrapping. Undefined/composite DataReply statuses are rejected.
Mapper contract errors can now fail builds; see docs/analyzers.md and the changelog for migration guidance.

Full notes: https://github.com/lobodava/artisan-orm/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageId>Artisan.ORM</PackageId>
    <Product>Artisan.ORM</Product>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <!-- Deterministic / reproducible builds and SourceLink -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    <PackageOutputPath>$(OutputPath)</PackageOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\Logo.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="LICENSE.txt" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="7.1.1" />
    <!-- SqlClient still permits vulnerable PKCS versions. Publish these minimums to consumers. -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="8.0.2" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' != 'net10.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="9.0.21" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Folder Include="Properties\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Artisan.Orm.Analyzers\Artisan.Orm.Analyzers.csproj"
                      OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Resolve the analyzer output at pack time, after the project reference has built. -->
  <Target Name="IncludeArtisanAnalyzers" BeforeTargets="_GetPackageFiles">
    <MSBuild Projects="..\Artisan.Orm.Analyzers\Artisan.Orm.Analyzers.csproj"
             Targets="GetTargetPath" Properties="Configuration=$(Configuration);TargetFramework=netstandard2.0">
      <Output TaskParameter="TargetOutputs" ItemName="ArtisanAnalyzerAssembly" />
    </MSBuild>
    <PropertyGroup>
      <ArtisanAnalyzerDirectory>@(ArtisanAnalyzerAssembly->'%(RootDir)%(Directory)')</ArtisanAnalyzerDirectory>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
      <None Include="@(ArtisanAnalyzerAssembly)" Pack="true" PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs" />
      <None Include="$(ArtisanAnalyzerDirectory)**\Artisan.Orm.Analyzers.resources.dll"
            Pack="true" PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs/%(RecursiveDir)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
